{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222113-setting-lingo-and-fun-with-slang","id":1222113,"title":"Setting Lingo and Fun With Slang","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-25T15:02:18-07:00","id":1222113,"title":"Setting Lingo and Fun With Slang","content":"Listening to the latest Ken and Robin Talk About Stuff and they're discussing creating slang for settings and it got me wondering. Obviously the Exalted writers over the years have done so, but have you ever found slang and lingo forming naturally at your own table? I'm curious to see what and how other people have come up with. <br /> <br /> Starting things off, I was running a 2E campaign that started with a variation of the Locust Crusade. The first sign the PCs found was corpses from a fight, a number of which had openings where the Soul Gems had been removed from Autochtonian casualties. It ended up leading to the creation of &quot;Slothead&quot; as a derogatory term for Authochthonians in that game's version of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T16:01:24-07:00","id":1222120,"title":"","content":"Makes sense<br /> <br /> I don't recall any specific terms that my players have come up with - but... considering the 'highly utilitarian ethics' then I'm sure they'll come up with some for, say, people they don't need or don't like","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T02:19:40-07:00","id":1222189,"title":"","content":"Using &quot;Yu-Shan!&quot; as an exclamation because it really lends itself well to that. Also, &quot;I swear to Yu-Shan you're the biggest moron I've ever met!&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> Servant of Infallible Location is commonly referred to as &quot;Findie Birdie&quot; including by the sorcerer summoning it. <br /> <br /> Abyssals have the ability to sense creatures of death and deathy phenomena in a wide radius. Since it's a modern setting and the characters are aware of sonar technology, they've taken to calling this &quot;pinging&quot;. <br /> <br /> Lunar friend going through a really unsubtle Limit Break on the full moon has got the &quot;moon crazies&quot; again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T03:42:00-07:00","id":1222198,"title":"","content":"As the first meeting with both Fae and Dream-Eaten was with a slave-trafficking network in Chiaroscuro, my players have used to call the Dream-Eaten &quot;Processed&quot;, as it was the euphemism that the merchant used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T06:57:02-07:00","id":1222233,"title":"","content":"Anyone who is impersonating one of the PCs specifically is a &quot;Queen Doppelpopolis.&quot; It's from a bit of dialogue from an episode of <i>Sealab 2021</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-26-2018, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:21:11-07:00","id":1222240,"title":"","content":"My current game is taking place on the Blessed Isle, and one of the players is a Dynast-gone-Solar. Dragons and their blood get used in A LOT of phrases, especially with the Solar's DB brother as part of the team. My personal favorite so far has been the euphemism &quot;thinning the blood&quot; used for sleeping with a commoner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T08:59:33-07:00","id":1222267,"title":"","content":"From a particularly irreverent Immaculate: &quot;Mela's tits!&quot; and &quot;Pasiap's Pillar!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12111-the_larz","name":"the_larz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T09:15:27-07:00","id":1222271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_larz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222113-setting-lingo-and-fun-with-slang?p=1222267#post1222267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a particularly irreverent Immaculate: &quot;Mela's tits!&quot; and &quot;Pasiap's Pillar!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In a similar (but even less Immaculate-approved) vein: &quot;Ahlat's horns!&quot; or if you're feeling filthy, &quot;Ahlat's horn!&quot;<br /> <br /> Awkward now that they've met Ahlat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T23:10:05-07:00","id":1222359,"title":"","content":"Stolen from someone right here on the forum was the term my Reckoner used to refer to those DBs who took the Coin and joined the Thousand Scales: \u201cCubicle dragons.\u201d I think I stole the term \u201clooking like a talent of jade\u201d as a Realm analog for \u201clooking like a million bucks,\u201d from this forum, too.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Jade, one original term cooked up in my most recent Exalted game came about when I mistakenly made reference to making change for a talent of jade, when I meant to say \u201cfinger of jade.\u201d When the GM rightly pointed out the difficulty involved in breaking a 32\u201d x 32\u201d slab of jade into 128 obols while whooping it up at a nightclub in Gem, I retconned my character as wearing a single Adamantine kneepad, specifically designed to make change from jade talents. After that, anyone who was ridiculously wealthy could be seen wearing a Jade-Breaking Kneepad, and wealthy folks in general came to be known as \u201ckneepads.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T11:03:06-07:00","id":1486049,"title":"","content":"The language and speech, especially the jargon, <a href=\"https://slangsearch.org/\" target=\"_blank\">slang search</a>, or argot, of a particular field, group, or individual: gamblers' lingo. language or speech, especially if strange or foreign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25083,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25083-antivdovich65621","user":"antivdovich65621","date":". 04-07-2023, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25083-antivdovich65621","name":"antivdovich65621","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T11:06:44-07:00","id":1486050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>antivdovich65621</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1222113-setting-lingo-and-fun-with-slang?p=1486049#post1486049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The language and speech, especially the jargon, slang, or argot, of a particular field, group, or individual: gamblers' lingo. language or speech, especially if strange or foreign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, You can find all kinds of slang at slang search.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25083-antivdovich65621","name":"antivdovich65621","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}